1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:07,137
This video shows you how to keep steps that several pipelines need in one place,

2
00:00:07,137 --> 00:00:09,150
and call them from each.

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,922
Two pipelines read tutorial-in: tutorial-in-parse and checkout-parse.

4
00:00:13,922 --> 00:00:19,830
Both should stamp each record with the ECS version, from the Elastic Common Schema.

5
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,907
Rather than add the same step to both, put it in a pipeline of its own.

6
00:00:24,907 --> 00:00:27,350
Add a pipeline called stamp-ecs.

7
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:33,422
Give it one Eval step: ecs.version is 8.11.

8
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:41,606
Save it, on a new branch called stamp-ecs.

9
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:48,057
Open tutorial-in-parse, and add a Call step at its end.

10
00:00:48,057 --> 00:00:51,812
At that point it runs stamp-ecs's steps.

11
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:05,820
Save, and do the same in checkout-parse.

12
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:16,592
Route the checkout sample.

13
00:01:16,592 --> 00:01:20,338
Each record now carries ecs.version.

14
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:23,376
Now the version changes.

15
00:01:23,376 --> 00:01:28,684
Edit it once, in stamp-ecs, to 8.17, and save.

16
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,150
Route the sample again.

17
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:34,185
The record carries 8.17.

18
00:01:34,185 --> 00:01:39,830
tutorial-in-parse calls stamp-ecs too, so it carries it as well.

19
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:43,103
Open it for review, and deploy it.

20
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,433
Check on learning.

21
00:01:51,633 --> 00:01:54,393
You change a step in stamp-ecs.

22
00:01:54,393 --> 00:01:57,041
Which pipelines change?

23
00:02:01,441 --> 00:02:03,708
Every pipeline that calls it.

24
00:02:03,708 --> 00:02:07,670
Here, tutorial-in-parse and checkout-parse.

25
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:12,265
Next, run pipelines on a worker group.
